<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bhavadeva Bhatta</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">11th–12th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bhavadeva Bhatta was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> scholar and minister of King Harivarman of the Varman dynasty of eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>. He wrote treatises on Vedic ritual, Mimamsa philosophy and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> law, among them works on rites and penances used in Bengal for centuries. A long inscription from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhubaneswar">Bhubaneswar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odisha">Odisha</a>, recording his family and building of a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vishnu">Vishnu</a> temple, is a key source for the Varman dynasty.</p></div>
